=== 1. Manual run against this machine's real database (first run) ===
$ dotnet run --project src/Merchandising.Maintenance -- seed

Seeding from 'C:\Users\Admin\Documents\Hardware_Merchandising_System\db\seed\seed-data.json'...
  categories  5 created, 0 already present
  brands      3 created, 0 already present
  units       3 created, 0 already present
  products    8 created, 0 already present
  suppliers   3 created, 0 already present
  accounts    4 created, 1 already present

  NEW ACCOUNT CREDENTIALS - shown once, never printed again:
    SuperAdmin           superadmin           <redacted - 24 random chars>
    ProcurementOfficer   procurementofficer   <redacted - 24 random chars>
    InventoryClerk       inventoryclerk       <redacted - 24 random chars>
    Cashier              cashier              <redacted - 24 random chars>
New account credentials appended to 'C:\ProgramData\MerchandisingSystem\config\installation-credentials.txt'.

  [PASS] Completes without error (Done-when box 1)

Note: "accounts 4 created, 1 already present" - a user named "admin" already
existed on this machine from a manual session on 2026-08-22, predating this
card, with role SuperAdmin already assigned. The seed command correctly
found it by username and left it untouched rather than erroring or
duplicating it - exactly the "idempotent by key" behaviour the Done-when
boxes ask for. A genuinely clean clone has no such row, so all five accounts
would be created there. Confirmed by the automated test in section 3 below,
which asserts EXISTENCE of the five usernames rather than which role each
happens to carry, for exactly this reason.

