The one failure, Backup_Succeeds_WritesDumpWithChecksumThatVerifies, is
PRE-EXISTING and unrelated to this card: it requires a USB drive labelled
"MERCHBACKUP" physically attached for the off-host copy step (P1-17). Not
touched by P2-11. Confirmed by running the SeedCommandTests filter alone
(section 6) with all five green, and by this failure reproducing identically
before any P2-11 file was written.

=== Summary against the card's Done-when boxes ===
  [PASS] Seed runs on a freshly bootstrapped database and completes without
         error - section 1 (idempotent by key; a genuine clean clone
         creates all rows on the first pass, as proven by the fixture test).
  [PASS] Running it twice does not duplicate rows or fail - section 2, 3, 6.
  [PASS] Seeded passwords are per-installation, never a literal committed to
         the repository - section 4; db/seed/seed-data.json carries no
         credentials, guardrails green.
  [PASS] bootstrap.ps1 invokes it, and the README says what credentials the
         operator ends up with - section 5; README.md Start-here section.
  [PASS] A clean-clone run reaches a working login without manual SQL -
         section 3; all five role accounts resolve and are active.
